"reasoning": "The patient presents with fever, headache, swollen lymph nodes, weakness, and fatigue. These symptoms are highly characteristic of a viral upper respiratory infection. Swollen lymph nodes (lymphadenopathy) combined with fever, headache, and generalized fatigue/weakness are classic signs of the body's immune response to a common viral pathogen. While other conditions like dengue or malaria can cause fever and headache, they typically present with additional specific symptoms such as severe body/joint pain, rash, or chills, which are absent here. The combination of symptoms aligns best with the common cold among the provided diagnostic options.",
"final_answer": "[DIAGNOSIS]common cold[/DIAGNOSIS]"
